    <description>The Apollo 12 Lunar Module (LM) ''Intrepid'' was the second crewed vehicle to land on the Moon. The Apollo 12 LM was a two-stage (descent and ascent) vehicle designed for space operations near and on the Moon. It carried two astronauts and the Apollo 12 Lunar Surface Experiments Package (ALSEP), which contained scientific experiments to be deployed and left on the lunar surface and other scientific and sample collection apparatus.  </description>
